<ix:nonNumeric contextRef="d_2024-11-01_2025-10-31" name="ecd:CompActuallyPaidVsTotalShareholderRtnTextBlock" id="c65" escape="true">
<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"><b><a id="relcomppaid" href="#"></a>Relationship Between Compensation Actually Paid and Company Performance</b></p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

<p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;text-indent:27pt;">The following graphs show the relationship between the compensation actually paid to our PEO and our Non-PEO NEO to our total shareholder return and net income (loss) over the three fiscal years ended October 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023. For purposes of calculating total shareholder return in the chart below, the last reported sales price of the Company&#8217;s Common Shares as of October 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023 was $7.87, $2.45 and $2.71, respectively.&#160;As of February __, 2026, the last reported sales price of the Company&#8217;s Common Shares was $___ per share.</p>

<p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p>

